course: dictionary
lesson: 4817
title: Hunger: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hunger can mean more than one thing, so the context tells you which meaning you need. Read the sentence around it, then ask which meaning fits. «Hunger shows as a rumbling tummy, low energy, grumpiness and trouble paying attention.» Here hunger is the feeling your body gives when it needs food.
explain: In sentences about the world, hunger can mean something much more serious. «Cockroaches survive more radiation than people but are not indestructible: cold, heat and hunger still kill them.» Here hunger is a serious lack of food, which can kill.
explain: A hunger for something means a strong wish for it. «The British suffragettes went on hunger strike in prison» to show how determined they were. Check each sentence: is hunger a body feeling, a serious lack, or a strong wish?
fact: Hunger is a noun. Formal writing can also use it as a verb, as in «hunger for» something.
fact: Hunger is the body's signal that it needs energy. A healthy breakfast helps you learn.
fact: «Die of hunger» means to die because there is not enough food.
fact: «Hunger for knowledge» means a strong wish to learn.
fact: «Hunger pangs» are sudden, sharp feelings of hunger in your tummy.
exercise: «Hunger shows as a rumbling tummy, low energy, grumpiness and trouble paying attention.» In this sentence, what is hunger? | A type of insect | A wish to travel to far places | *The feeling your body gives when it needs food | A kind of cold weather
exercise: Many people in the world suffer from hunger for a long time. What does hunger mean here? | *A serious lack of food that makes people ill | Being tired after a long day at school | A strong wish for a new bike | A rumbling tummy before lunch
exercise: Find and copy the phrase that means a strong wish to learn. | feel hunger | hunger strike | die of hunger | *hunger for knowledge
test: In «a hunger for adventure», what does hunger mean? | A serious lack of food | *A strong wish for something | A rumbling tummy
test: Which phrase means refusing food as a protest? | *Hunger strike | Feel hunger | Hunger pangs
exam: Jayden reads, «Cockroaches survive more radiation than people, but cold, heat and hunger still kill them.» Which meaning of hunger fits best? | *A serious lack of food, which can kill | Being full after a big dinner | A strong wish for food | A feeling of tiredness after school
